version, but you are not obliged to do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete
the exception statement you do not extend from your version.

What this does not do
---------------------

It grants you nothing with respect to Adobe's code. Obtaining either SDK, and
complying with whatever agreement Adobe attaches to it, remains entirely
between you and Adobe. These exceptions only remove the GPL's objection to the
combination; they do not create a right to the other half of it.

They also do not weaken the GPL over StrokeMaster itself. The source in this
repository, the ExtendScript in tools/jsx/ (which links nothing and never
needed an exception in the first place), and any modification you make to
either, stay GPL-3.0-or-later.
